 "prompt": "Write a short, plain-language note to a new team member explaining what a code review is for, what a reviewer looks at, and how to respond to comments.",
 "prompt_text": "[gMASK]<sop><|user|>Write a short, plain-language note to a new team member explaining what a code review is for, what a reviewer looks at, and how to respond to comments.<|assistant|><think></think>",
 "completion_text": "# Welcome to the Team: Code Reviews 101\n\nHi! Here's a quick rundown on code reviews, since you'll be doing them a lot here.\n\n## What a code review is for\n\nA code review is when a teammate reads your code before it's merged into the main codebase. It's not a test or a judgment of you \u2014 it's how we:\n\n- Catch bugs and mistakes early\n- Keep the codebase consistent and readable\n- Share knowledge, so more than one person understands each part of the system\n- Improve code quality for everyone, including future-you\n\n## What a reviewer looks at\n\nReviewers focus on things like:\n\n- **Correctness** \u2014 Does the code do what it's supposed to? Are there edge cases or bugs?\n- **Readability** \u2014 Can someone else understand it easily? Are names clear?\n- **Tests** \u2014 Are there tests, and do they cover the important cases?\n- **Consistency** \u2014 Does it follow the patterns and style we already use?\n- **Security and performance** \u2014 Any obvious risks or slowdowns?\n\nReviewers generally *don't* nitpick personal style preferences. If something is purely subjective, it's usually fine to just discuss it.\n\n## How to respond to comments\n\n- **Don't take it personally.** Comments are about the code, not about you.\n- **Reply to every comment**, even if it's just \"Done\" or \"Good catch, fixed.\"\n- **Push back politely if you disagree.** Say why \u2014 e.g., \"I did it this way because X.\" Disagreements are normal; we talk them through.\n- **Ask questions if a comment is unclear.** \"Could you say more about what you mean here?\" is always okay.\n- **Keep changes small.** If a comment asks for a big rework, it's fine to discuss scope first.\n\n",
